@Lolchu These are called 5,7-ring defects. 

The bonding of the sidewall of CNTs is really a delocalised sp2 network.

When you interrupt the aromaticity of an area (i.e. a 5,7-ring defect) you are change one (or more) carbons in those rings to sp3 - and cause the CNT to bend or twist 👇 https://t.co/3zFWZ1fris

